{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the man shall be cleared of guilt.</b> If the waters examined her, let him not fear to say, 'I have sinned in her death' — he is clear of punishment. Another interpretation: from the time he makes her drink, she is permitted to him, and he is cleared of guilt — for the sotah is forbidden to her husband (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:36.578221924Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}